{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not murder.</b> Whether by hand, whether by tongue, whether by silence — for example, if the secret of a murderer was revealed to you and you do not reveal the secret. And this language of רציחה applies only to an unlawful death, but the language of מיתה and the language of הריגה apply whether lawfully or unlawfully." "<b>[You shall not murder.</b> A punishment for murder we have heard; a warning, from where? Scripture says: you shall not murder.]" "<b>You shall not commit adultery.</b> Lest you say: it is forbidden to minimize the commandments, for I have been warned against murder, but to multiply and add is permitted — even in relations with a married woman and all other forbidden relations. Therefore it says: you shall not commit adultery. And ניאוף conveys an act of transgression."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:03.562881940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}